he human race  the church of the final atonement had  granted many believers the opportunity  to enter into strike territory  undertaking the pilgrimage on the world  of hyperion  only death had waited for them our seven  pilgrims in the beginning of this series  are believed to be the final seven who  will ever take this pilgrimage  due to the fact that the anti-entropic  fields surrounding the time tombs  are expanding and the strike's territory  is increasing  whereas previously it had been bound to  a single area on hyperion  each of the pilgrims has a different  reason for journeying into strike  territory  though they are all going into it with  the understanding that they will all  likely die  during his 11 years as consul on that  distant and enigmatic  world the mysterious church of the  strike  had allowed a dozen barges of off-world  pilgrims to depart for  the wind-swept barons around the time  tombs north of the mountains  no one had returned the seven pilgrims  are as follows  father hoyt a priest of the catholic  church  colonel fedman cassad a former soldier  of force  the hegemony's military a poet by the  name of martin salinas  who had been born on earth before its  destruction  saw weintraub and his now infant  daughter rachel  who has a strange illness which forces  her to age backwards in time  ron lamia a private investigator who had  been rescued by the church of the final  atonement  marin aspic the consul and hetmasteen  a templar who is in fact the captain of  the living tree ship which transports  them  to the world of hyperion the first book  in the hyperion cantos is based on the  structure of jeffrey chaucer's  canterbury tells  during their journey each of the seven  pilgrims takes turns  recounting the strange events which led  them to be on the strike pilgrimage  at the same time these seven partake in  the pilgrimage  an ouster attack is underway the ousters  were among the humans in the universe  not under the influence of the galactic  hegemony  the ousters had inhabited many different  kinds of worlds  and augmented themselves to fit the  various environments in which they lived  which caused them to seem less human to  the members of the hegemony  the first book in the series concludes  after each of the seven pilgrims  have finished recounting their harrowing  tales each of which unveils more about  this universe  the world of hyperion plays some key  role in each of the stories  at the end of the book the pilgrims are  finally approaching the time tombs  known to be guarded by the being known  as the strike  after a long and dangerous journey on  the world of hyperion  during an ouster attack from above the  second book  fall of hyperion starts up directly  following the events of the first book  and concludes the story of the seven  pilgrims  thank you guys for watching make sure  you like and subscribe for more science  fiction lore  you

